/target
/tmp/
/.cargo/
/Cargo.lock
# Local configs containing keys — NEVER commit them.
# Rules are anchored to the root (leading "/"), so EACH location must be listed
# separately: on Windows, the data directory is next to the exe, while running the build from the
# repository root creates these files here as well.
/config.toml
/config.enc
/servers.enc
/settings.toml
# Terminal working directories: settings (`cfg/`), databases (`data/`), and config snapshots
# (`backups/`; may contain API keys; retention is defined by `config::backup`).
/cfg/
/data/
/backups/
# Cargo.lock is local and ignored: the terminal uses the current Git dependencies
# from the public Cargo.toml, while local development can override MoonUI via .cargo/config.toml.
/legasy
*.log
/docAi
# Benchmark outputs (sample/summary CSV files) are local; do not commit them.
/tools/bench-out/
# GPUI migration labs: a gpui-component clone for the gates (Gate 0/Lab 1/2/3).
# This large local testbed is not part of the product; do not commit it.
/vendor/
render_diag.log
# Private working docs (handoffs, sin log, design, baseline screenshots, OLD archives) —
# only on this machine and NEVER included in the public repo. Only purely architectural
# docs/ remain public (RENDER_INVALIDATION, REFACTOR_RENDER, ARCHITECTURE_MULTICORE).
/docs-internal/
# Internal agent instructions and working notes remain on disk (the agent reads them
# locally) but are NEVER committed to the public repo. Removed from history (filter-repo).
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
/DisQuestions
# Shared agent entry points and implementations STAY tracked:
# .claude/settings.json, .codex/hooks.json, and .agent-hooks/.
# Only the following per-machine Claude settings, runtime locks, and skills are ignored.
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
/.claude/skills/
